+/** Measured full-page base64 payload per shape variant, sized to the TYPICAL
+ *  page rather than the worst one. Byte weight tracks glyph ink per page, not
+ *  cell area — a CJK `silver16-bw` page weighs ~570 KB while a `5x8-bw` page of
+ *  the same canvas sits near 50 KB — so these are per-variant measurements over
+ *  persisted frames rather than a formula.
+ *  {@link FRAME_DATA_BYTES_ESTIMATE} matches the small-glyph `bw` shapes the
+ *  legacy single estimate was calibrated on.
+ *
+ *  Why typical and not worst-case: this value divides the per-request byte
+ *  budget, so it decides how many frames get planned. Calibrating on the
+ *  largest observed page would plan three frames where twenty-five actually
+ *  fit at the common edge — permanent history loss on every compaction.
+ *  Sizing to the typical page plans the count the budget really holds.
+ *  Outliers stay covered because estimates only size the plan:
+ *  `shedFramesOverBudget` re-checks the real rendered bytes and drops from the
+ *  oldest end when dense content (JSON dumps, CJK) renders heavier than the
+ *  typical page. */
